.TH CYAML_STR_VAL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_str_val \- extract a string value from a CYAML_STRING node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_str_val(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return a read-only pointer to the null-terminated string stored in
node.  Calls fatal_err() if node is NULL or its type is not
CYAML_STRING.

The returned pointer is owned by the node; it is invalidated when the
node is destroyed or its value is changed via cyaml_set().
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  CYAML_STRING node.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Pointer to the internal string buffer.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_type (3),
.BR cyaml_create_string (3)
